  "slug": "modeling-connectivity-8f3f",
  "summary": "Structural and diffusion-derived priors are being built into neuroimaging registration and modeling pipelines to extract disease-relevant variation.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the use of explicit structural representations to extract disease-relevant variation from neuroimaging data. JOSAConn is the clearest connectivity-guided case, adding dMRI tractography-derived connectivity maps to deep-learning cortical surface registration and reported to outperform FreeSurfer. The hippocampal tau PET framework instead relies on principal surface geometry, pairing two-stage inverse-probability-weighted regression and SuStaIn subtyping with choroid plexus contamination detection. TRAECR addresses PET preprocessing for statistical modeling through registration, MRI co-registration, and COMBAT/RAVEL harmonization, and the TBI work targets heterogeneity across multi-site segmentations. Connectivity is not shared across these items; what is new is surface geometry and tractography-derived connectivity serving as inputs to modeling.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2025-11-09"
}
